WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:09.760
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:20.290
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.480
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:06.960
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:14.230
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:20.970
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.490
I have lived all this time
without ever making a decision.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.240
This is my punishment.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.960
I failed to become an eternal maiden.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.330
And I failed to make my way to
that other world. I remained here.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.710
Never to touch another.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.350
Never to feel another’s
embrace. And still…

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.720
I remain here.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.640
But why?

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.220
Why did they do that to your body?

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.530
Because I refused to
choose a permanent gender…

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.230
…they sentenced me to become
the gatekeeper of the Spring.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.520
Because you wouldn’t choose?

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.800
So that no future maiden
would make the same mistake.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.450
To stand here for all time…

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.950
That is my penance for
running away from reality.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:45.470
<b>Choices</b>

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:50.480
Chor Tempest is to be
officially disbanded.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.520
Sibyllae, we have decided that it is
now time for you to go to the Spring.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.480
What?

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.400
Just a moment!

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.490
Why are we also being stripped
of our posts as sibyllae?

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.990
You will be ceding your duties
to the Plumbum priestesses.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.280
No way!

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.490
Father!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.680
They won’t even let us be Simoun
sibyllae anymore? Then that means…

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.710
We’ll have to leave the Arcus Prima!

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.300
Is that what you’re saying?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.930
Well, forcing them to make a
decision like that so suddenly…

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.130
We can hardly expect them to
choose on such short notice!

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.720
They need time to prepare.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.130
We are out of time.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.600
All we’re asking for is a short period.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.270
Compared to the long history
of Simulacrum Kyuukoku…

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.100
…it would only be a fleeting moment.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.610
Sibylla Morinas…

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.320
You heard what’s happening to us, right?

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.450
Yes.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.450
Are you happy now?

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.410
Actually…

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.460
I’m going to be leaving
the Arcus Prima as well.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.760
Kyuukoku won’t be flying
the Simouns any longer.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.720
And to prove it, the entire maintenance
crew is being moved to the highlands.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.300
What?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.720
It’s all the same to us
no matter where we end up.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.980
The Simouns are the
divine vessels of the gods.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.060
And yet…

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.360
No matter how close I try to get…

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.150
No, the truth is that I’ve
discovered something about myself.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.740
I no longer care about the Simouns!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.740
As long as I know you’re safe,
that’s enough to make me happy.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.830
Go ahead and despise me now.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.800
They’re getting smaller, aren’t they?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:51.060
I wanted to become a man and putter
around with you and the Simouns, but…

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:15.250
Which are you going to choose?

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.280
I guess you’ve always
wanted to become a man, huh?

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.460
You probably couldn’t care less that
we’re being forced to go to the Spring.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.470
That’s right. You’ve always…

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.970
That’s so not true!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.970
I’m scared too!

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.180
It scares me that we
have to grow up now!

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.060
I want to lean on someone else…

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.480
I want someone to protect me! But…

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.480
Alty…

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.270
Oh, shut up, you dummy!

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.230
What a dummy you are, Big Sister!

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.530
Dummy!

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:52.240
Dummy… dummy… dummy… dummy!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.290
Picking a fight with your sister?
I mean, how immature is that?

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.340
You’re still just kids. You’re
both too young to become adults.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:12.100
Hey, Vura, all the Chor Rubor girls
already picked their genders, right?

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.630
The ones who had a family
business to take over became male.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.470
The others, well, it was pretty random.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.390
Oh?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.440
What about you, Floe?

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:24.310
Me? Whatever. I don’t really
care which I end up being!

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:27.190
Of course, if I were in love, I would
be telling a different story, but…

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:31.200
Really? But everyone says that
you’ve got a thing for Aer.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.720
Right, and I’ve told them over
and over that it’s not true!

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.540
Oh, for heaven’s sake.
What does it matter, anyway?

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:38.910
But I don’t know…

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:41.960
For some reason I feel so lonely.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:45.960
That’s what growing up is all about.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.970
So if you feel lonely,
it means you’ve grown up?

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.980
I just remembered something.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.440
Alty was such a moron!

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.790
Darn it, didn’t I tell
you not to tag along?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:11.070
You’re always slowing me down, Alty!

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.070
And you’re such a dummy, Big Sister!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.290
Who are you calling a dummy?
You clumsy slowpoke!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.790
Dummy!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.540
Whatever! You can find your
own way back then, you wimp!

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:24.750
Dummy!

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.260
Dummy!

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.510
You’re such a dummy, Big Sister!

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.420
Even if we were in the
middle of a fight…

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.940
…she could never come up
with any names to call me.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.040
She could never say
anything except, “Dummy!”

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.900
And the thing is she never learned.
She just kept following me.

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:55.410
I mean, really… What a
little moron of a sister I have!

00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:00.080
I wonder when it was
that Alty stopped being…

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.920
…such a little wimp.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:06.080
I’m going to protect you, Big Sister.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:10.420
She got such an assertive look
in her eyes, and she grew so tall.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:14.970
It was like she suddenly became
more of a grownup than me.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:19.520
But because so much was
going on, I didn’t even notice.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.940
To me, Alty was still
the same little wimp.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.730
And I’ve always averted my gaze from
her. I just didn’t want to believe it.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.520
Even so… I…

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.940
You’ll be forgiven.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:35.450
Even if you’re no longer a sibylla, that
doesn’t mean you can’t do certain things.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.950
Like forgiving one another…

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.950
To forgive someone for wronging you…

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.450
…and to be forgiven in return.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.960
If we can manage to do that much…

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.960
…I think we can still call ourselves
sibyllae even after we choose our gender.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.380
Listen…

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.260
I really do like you, Para-sama.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:59.970
My feelings for you won’t change
whether I become a man or a woman.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.970
I don’t think I’ll ever
stop looking up to you!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.690
Thank you.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.490
They say that the high priestess
has been driven from the Arcus Prima.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.250
Aer, we don’t have much time. You…

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.450
What do you want me to say?

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:27.560
Never mind, don’t answer
that. I already know.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.630
But…

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.500
I’m never gonna do it!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.210
Aer?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:36.470
You just want to see Amuria again. That’s
why you want to go to the other world!

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:40.220
I can’t do a Ri Majon with you
if that’s all you care about!

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:47.560
Why did Onasia show that to me?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.730
Never to feel another’s embrace.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.230
And still…

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.030
…I remain here.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.320
Onasia… Is she doomed
to stand there forever?

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:03.290
Never to know forgiveness?

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.180
Never to be saved?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.750
Yun?

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.800
I thought that I should take
some of Mamina’s things with me.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.010
Oh. Her trunk is under her bed.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:23.640
When I go home, I’ll be
seeing Mamina’s mother, so…

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.850
I thought I could give them to her then.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.460
Still smells like Mamina!

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.280
It’s not much…

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.360
…but I hope Mamina’s mother
will find comfort in this.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:40.360
I wonder… Is it even possible
for us to save anybody now?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.270
I’m sure it will be very difficult.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.120
We can barely take care
of ourselves as it is.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.920
But if we try our utmost,
then maybe we can save…

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.420
…at least one person in this world.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.210
One person…

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.880
Yun, is there someone in your life?

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.890
That one person?

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:07.390
Yun’s gone?

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:12.100
Yes. I hear the highland soldiers
are looking for her, but…

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.400
Why, Yun?

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.730
Maybe she decided she
didn’t want to grow up.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.900
No, not Yun.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.110
She…

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.910
She must have realized…

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:23.700
What?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.660
Oh, nothing.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.160
Oh, whatever! Being
such a stranger to us!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.160
She just got up and left
without saying a word!

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.680
I know…

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:34.170
…but once Chor Tempest is disbanded,
we’ll all be going our separate ways.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.180
I have something to tell you all.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:46.300
About another world…

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:11.600
No way! Who knew the Emerald Ri
Majon could do something like that!

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:15.960
Right, but that’s precisely
what’s going to save us.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.970
Each of us is going to
choose a gender soon.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:25.720
And our days on the Arcus
Prima will come to an end.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:30.560
But those two won’t be choosing a
gender and will stay the way they are…

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.230
Not choose a gender…

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.270
…and stay the way they are?

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.780
When the rest of us are all grown up…

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:42.780
…and the emotions we carry
inside us now have faded…

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.240
Those two will be
alive in another era…

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:50.990
…somewhere in a sparkling world,
looking just as they do now.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.750
I need to talk to you.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.760
I get it. So those two will always…

00:12:58.760 --> 00:12:59.770
Right.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.070
Even after we’ve all become adults…

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:05.260
…they’ll stay the same
for us for all time, right?

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.260
The “eternal present”…

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:14.520
You don’t have to go to the other
world with me if you don’t want to.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.270
But whatever it is we decide,
we really should tell the others.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.940
That we’re not going to the Spring…

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.150
I don’t need you to tell me that!

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.740
I do want to know what
happened to Amuria.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.620
I do want to see her again.

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.950
I can’t lie to you about that.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.660
But…

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:41.840
The one I’m in love with…

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.130
…is you.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:51.140
The one who lives facing life, rather
than death… It’s you whom I love.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:56.140
The one who rescued me from the
darkness… It’s you whom I love.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.600
The thought of going to that
other world frightens me.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:02.020
But if you and I are
together, then I’m sure…

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.360
Hold on.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:09.500
It’s not that I wanted you to tell
me all about your feelings for me!

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.080
You don’t need to give me an answer.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.200
I just thought that
I should let you know.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.540
No…

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.750
I wanted to let you know. That’s all.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.500
Nothing more.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:37.380
How am I supposed to take
that in all of a sudden?

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:40.690
I don’t understand!

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:45.360
The one I’m in love with… is you.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.330
Why is it…

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.070
…so painful?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:37.080
To save the drifting spirits
of my fallen comrades…

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.960
That’s the one thing I’ve
always had on my mind.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.790
But deep down, I always knew the truth.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.840
That it’s not possible
to save the dead…

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:49.630
But still…

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.170
There’s one who even I…

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.090
No…

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:57.600
What I realized was that there’s one
person who can only be saved by me.

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:07.540
For some reason, I’d hoped…

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:11.440
…to hear those very words from you.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:16.700
I never chose a gender for myself.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.450
But…

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.750
I was not able to hold
on to my maiden’s soul.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:26.540
And now, once again,
I am trying to escape.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.960
This time burdening you with
all my responsibilities…

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:31.920
No.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:36.600
You’re beautiful.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:09.070
You’re beautiful…

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.730
I can hear quite a commotion out there.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:57.220
That voice… it must be Sibylla Floe.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:05.880
Aer, were you planning
to stay in bed all day?

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:08.630
It’s our last day on the Arcus Prima!

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.610
Wait for me, Alty!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:14.150
Not gonna happen!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.640
Please wait up!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.660
Up here!

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.200
It’s an amazing view!

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.920
Come on, dance with me, Aer!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.920
Huh? Uh, I…

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.270
Don’t tell me that’s…

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.140
Please, let the Messis
transport you to the Spring.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.140
Thanks, but it’s all right.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:35.980
I’ve always wanted to ride
on a helical-motor train.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.480
I understand.

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:42.240
May I ask what’s going on with
Sibylla Neviril and Sibylla Aer?

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.950
They have asked for a little more time.

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:48.450
Fine.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:50.710
All right then.

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:54.650
Farewell.

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:57.920
We’ll come back to say
hello when we’re adults!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.090
The mountains are getting closer!

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:41.510
It’s almost time for lunch.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.590
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:48.790
I had them pack us something to eat
before we left. Is anybody hungry?

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.850
Those look delicious!

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:53.600
Me too! Me too!

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.850
I’d like a vegetable sandwich.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.850
What about you, Roatre?

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:57.810
A meat sandwich for me, please!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:58.860
Same for me, please.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.360
Oh boy, I’m starving!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.690
This is so good!

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:06.760
Okay, this is for Roatre.
This one’s yours, Paraietta.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:07.620
Thanks.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:10.080
Man, why didn’t you tell us sooner that you had sandwiches?

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.540
Come on, Floe!

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:24.400
But that’s…

00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:27.400
Yun!

00:22:41.070 --> 00:22:47.780
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:52.020
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:59.090
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:06.690
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:19.580
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:24.750
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:28.730
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.730 --> 00:23:32.770
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:38.640
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:44.180
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.180 --> 00:23:47.610
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:53.280
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:59.510
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:05.640 --> 00:24:08.840
The girls embark on their
journey towards adulthood…

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:12.430
…as Neviril and Aer head
towards the “eternal present.”

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.430
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:19.930
<b>Pair</b>

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:17.470
Pair.
